[3638]="7005A7FF\n1\tTalk to Dáin\tDáin can be found at Amdân. Dáin has learned that King Thráin intends to call a council of the Kings of the Seven Houses at Amdân and has asked you to join him. You should talk to Dáin.\n2\tTalk to Dáin at Amdân\tDáin can be found at Amdân. After attending the council of the Kings of the Seven Houses, you took rest before the battle ahead. You should talk to Dáin.\n",
[3639]="7002EE37\n1\tComplete Support Góda\030Complete Support Ingmar\tLord Ingmar and Lady Góda are within the Mead Hall of Eaworth. Reeve Ingbert has asked you to speak with both Lady Góda and Lord Ingmar to learn their positions, so that you may better advise him.\n2\tTalk to Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tReeve Ingbert awaits you in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. You should return to Reeve Ingbert and give him your counsel.\n",
[3640]="7000AC4F\n1\tDefeat First Marshal Án\tThe Free Peoples' encampment is somewhere to the east of Tol Ascarnen. Paashum sent you to the enemy encampment of Tol Ascarnen to find and defeat First Marshal Án. You should not attempt this alone as Án is a powerful combatant.\n2\tReturn to Soldier Paashum at the encampment north-east of Tol Ascarnen\tThe Angmar-encampment is somewhere to the west of Tol Ascarnen. A successful assault against the Free Peoples' encampment resulted in the slaughter of the First Marshal and many of the forces located in the encampment east of Tol Ascarnen.\n",
[3641]="7006D19C\n1\tRaise Ambarûli banners (total: 6)\tAs you secure sections of the Wrackwade, raise Ambarûli banners to lay claim to them.\n2\tDefeat Obonákh\tYou have reclaimed the span of the Wrackwade in the name of Ambarûl, and now the Ordâkhai have put forth their champion to challenge you. You should defeat their champion.\n",
[3642]="70026E56\n1\tThe people of Lhan Tarren can be found throughout the village. You should speak with the members of the Stag-clan to remind them to be present at the Feast of the Running Stag. Their presence will ease the Elder's worry that his clan has grown soft and weak.\t\n2\tReturn to the Elder of Lhan Tarren\tThe Elder awaits you in the village of Lhan Tarren. You should return to the Elder and tell him that you spoke gentle reminders to many of the villagers.\n",
[3643]="70044D68\n1\tSpeak with Rastion in the Middle Stores\tThe Middle Stores are in the southern part of the Third Circle. You should speak with Rastion, the Middle Stores worker, before you start taking inventory there.\n2\tTally sacks of grain in the Middle Stores (total: 10)\030Defeat any rats you encounter (total: 10)\tThe Middle Stores are in the southern part of the Third Circle. You should tally sacks of grain in the Middle Stores and keep an eye out for any rats.\n3\tSpeak with Rastion\tThe Middle Stores are in the southern part of the Third Circle. You should speak with Rastion, and let him know that you are finished in the Middle Stores.\n4\tSpeak with Lintanar\tLintanar can be found in the northern part of the Third Circle. You should speak with Lintanar.\n",
[3644]="70045259\n1\tCollect paraffin (total: 8)\030Collect flint (total: 5)\tNarvellon the Beacon-keeper has asked you to gather flint and paraffin from the beacons of the Beacon Hills.\n2\tReturn to Narvellon\tYou should return to Narvellon in Ost Rimmon with the lighting supplies that you gathered from the beacons.\n",
[3645]="7002ED1E\n1\tGuards can be found throughout Eaworth. Pedwin wants you to bring flasks of ale to the guards of Eaworth in order to encourage them.\t\n2\tTalk to Pedwin at the Eaworth Vendor Hall\tPedwin is in the Eaworth Vendor Hall. You should return to Pedwin and let him know that you have done as he asked.\n",
[3646]="70037161\n1\tTalk to Torferth\030Talk to Dudsig\030Talk to Wilsig\030Talk to Tidric\030Talk to Sidnoth\tThe leaders of the people can be found at Thane Tordag's encampment, north of the road between Torsbury and Stoke. Thane Tordag has asked you to speak with the leaders of his people and rally their spirits to join him in his counterassault.\n2\tTalk to Thane Tordag at his encampment\tThane Tordag is at his encampment, north of the road between Torsbury and Stoke. You should return to Thane Tordag and let him know that his people and allies are all prepared to stand beside him at Torsbury.\n",
[3647]="70026E48\n1\tTalk to Lavaneth\tThe Huntsman's Hall is in the south of the Mournshaws. It can be entered through Tûm's portal or by crossing the river to the south. Tûm asked you to venture to the Huntsman's Hall and speak with those within.\n",
[3648]="7004D063\n1\tComplete the Reopening the Realm quest arc to continue\tYou should assist the Raft-elves of Loeglond. The Trail of Rust quest arc will continue after completing the Reopening the Realm quest arc which begins with Thranduil in Felegoth.\n2\tTalk to Thorlind in Loeglond\tYou should talk to Thorlind, who can be found in Loeglond.\n3\tTravel to Esgaroth-of-old\tYou should travel to Esgaroth-of-old, which is located east of Loeglond.\n4\tDefeat foes at Esgaroth-of-old (total: 6)\030Eavesdrop on thieves in Esgaroth-of-old\030Eavesdrop on look-outs in Esgaroth-of-old\tThe voices were coming from somewhere in the ruins of Esgaroth-of-old, upon the Long Lake. You should investigate the voices, listening when you can and defeating any foes to protect yourself and keep the way safe.\n5\tTalk to Thorlind at Esgaroth\tYou should talk to Thorlind, who can be found just outside of Esgaroth-of-old.\n",
})
